{
  "name": "swim",
  "//": "SWIMMING FORWARD: a front crawl. The hips pitch the body 70 degrees forward and lift it 0.3 m so the back rides near the surface instead of the head going under; the body rolls 12 degrees toward the pulling arm. Each arm reaches ahead, catches, pulls under the belly to the thigh, and recovers OUT TO THE SIDE with the elbow high -- not over the back, which the shoulder's 50 degree reach-behind limit (human.json armU poseLimit) would clamp. Arms half a cycle apart; a six-beat flutter kick, toes pointed, the knee bending on the up-beat. Rotations: hips = lean Z (+ = right) of pitch X (+ = forward) of roll Y; every other part = sweep Y of flex X of abduction Z. A hanging limb: X negative = forward/up, positive = back; Z negative = the RIGHT limb out from the side. Knees +X bend, elbows -X bend. Hips pos in decimetres. All six swim clips share one 1200 ms period and one playhead (pose.cpp, the swim family), so a blend of two directions strokes in step.",
